When a text control’s relevant value changes, Ladybird clamps both ends
of its selection, or its caret, against the new value. Gecko does the
same for both elements: TextControlState’s SelectionProperties::
SetMaxLength() re-runs SetStart() and SetEnd(), each of which clamps
against the new length. WebKit’s HTMLTextAreaElement::setValueCommon()
and Blink’s HTMLTextAreaElement::SetValueCommon() also clamp both ends
for a textarea reset (TextControlSetValueSelection::Clamp and kClamp).

For an input reset, WebKit’s HTMLInputElement::reset() and Blink’s
HTMLInputElement::ResetImpl() go through setValue() and SetValue(),
which move the caret to the end of the new value instead — so there too,
no offset is left past the end.
